# Titan

## Lore

The Titans are the most famous and glamorous of the Palladium giants: noble warriors who, like knights-errant, wander in pairs (seldom more than four) seeking adventure, fighting evil and righting wrongs, as they have for tens of thousands of years. Humanoids and giants alike count them demigods. An archaic race that survived the war against the Old Ones, they were the Elves'' staunchest allies for eons, until the Elf-Dwarf War tore them away; since then no Titan has called an Elf "friend".

They look like idealized humans on a giant scale - tan skin, warm eyes, golden, silver or brown hair and muscular builds - and keep a secret society reminiscent of the Knights Templar, so their numbers are unknown. Fewer than a hundred are believed to have visited Rifts Earth since the Coming of the Rifts, but the tales of their heroics, especially in the Dark Age, are many. Three are rumored to ride with Lord Coake against the Kingdom of Monsters in Calgary, and others have been reported in the Magic Zone, Mexico, Africa, France, Germany, Poland, India and China.

**Alignment:** Any, but strongly leans toward good: Principled (35%), Scrupulous (35%) and Unprincipled (20%).

**Height:** 12 to 14 feet (3.6 to 4.2 m). **Weight:** 600 to 1,000 pounds (270 to 450 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 1,000 years.

## GM Notes

Titans are compassionate, merciful and honorable, welcomed by good and downtrodden folk everywhere, and drawn sooner or later wherever evil creatures of magic and supernatural forces gather; the occasional Titan is evil. Traditional enemies are Gigantes, Jotan, Ogres, Trolls and wicked supernatural beings; allies are humans, Spirits of Light, Kukulcan dragons and all champions of good, and on Rifts Earth Cyber-Knights, True Atlanteans, Lyn-Srial, Zembahk and the Mystic Kuznya. A Titan with any experience likely carries a magic weapon, item or armor handed down as an heirloom, and also likes precision high-tech weapons, TW items and Vibro-Blades.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-titan');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-titan';

